        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(imessage): apply authoritative projection in anchorless recovery",
        "body": "Fixes openclaw/openclaw#104136\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\n`repairIMessageConversationAnchor()` recovered conversation anchors from exact-GUID `messages.history` rows but only overlaid `chat_id` / `chat_guid` / `chat_identifier`. It preserved stale notification `sender`, `destination_caller_id`, and `is_from_me`, which could:\n\n1. Route a direct reply at the local iMessage identity instead of the remote peer.\n2. Dispatch an outgoing row as inbound when history says `is_from_me: true` but the broken notification said `false`.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Build a complete **authoritative recovery projection** from exact-GUID history rows (sender, direction, conversation fields).\n- **Keep `destination_caller_id` optional** per imsg payload contract (ClawSweeper P1).\n- **Fail-closed** on incomplete/conflicting projections; **drop recovered `is_from_me: true` rows**.\n- **Removed unrelated `src/infra/restart.ts` diff** from this PR.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Current head:** `00a71e39`\n\n| Case | Result |\n|------|--------|\n| Stale local `+15550000001` sender → history `+15550000002` | repaired sender `+15550000002`, chat 42 |\n| History omits `destination_caller_id` (valid imsg payload) | still recovers; keeps notification destination |\n| History `is_from_me: true` with notification `false` | dropped (`recovered authoritative row is from-me`) |\n| Conflicting exact-GUID rows | dropped (`conflicting exact-GUID history projections`) |\n| **Whole-path:** repair → inbound decision → `buildIMessageInboundContext` | `To=imessage:+15550000002` (not local `+15550000001`) |\n\n**Tests:**\n```\npnpm exec vitest run extensions/imessage/src/monitor/conversation-repair.test.ts\n→ 13 passed\npnpm exec vitest run extensions/imessage/src/monitor/inbound-processing.test.ts\n→ 33 passed\n```\n\n**Lint:** oxlint + oxfmt on touched files — clean\n\n## Review\n\n- ClawSweeper P1 addressed: optional destination preserved, unrelated restart scope removed, whole-path reply-routing proof added\n- AI-assisted: Yes\n\n@clawsweeper re-review",
